{"id": "unknown-2026-07-23-008", "date": "2026-07-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["growth", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "ICRA projects 6.4-6.6% GDP growth for India in Q1 FY27", "content": "ICRA has projected India’s GDP to have grown by a healthy 6.4-6.6 per cent in Q1 FY27.\nHowever, this is weaker than 7.7 per cent in Q4 FY26 and reflects the impact of high energy and commodity prices and limited availability of inputs on the margins of some sectors.\nThe ICRA business activity monitor showed the YoY expansion in economic activity jumped to 12 per cent in June from 9.4 per cent in May.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/icra-projects-6-4-6-6-gdp-growth-for-india-in-q1-fy27-312009-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-23-009", "date": "2026-07-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Section 338 ends North America's nearshoring tariff certainty", "content": "President Donald Trump signed Section 338 proclamations adding a 50 per cent tariff on covered Canadian goods from August 19.\nThe White House said covered goods remain liable even if they originate under USMCA, affecting apparel tariff certainty.\nTexPro data shows US textile and apparel imports from Canada totalled $1.45 billion in CY 2025, including $519 million in apparel.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/section-338-ends-north-america-s-nearshoring-tariff-certainty-312008-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-23-010", "date": "2026-07-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India’s structural challenges threaten 2047 goal; growth strong: WTO", "content": "India’s FY28 real GDP growth is projected to be 6.8-7.2 per cent, but sustaining the economic performance needed to turn developed by 2047 will need addressing structural challenges, including high trade costs, regulatory complexity, infrastructure gaps and barriers to deeper global integration, the WTO noted.\nUse of non-tariff measures by some nations has constrained market access for Indian exporters.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-structural-challenges-threaten-2047-goal-growth-strong-wto-312007-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-23-011", "date": "2026-07-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Vietnam calls for stronger ASEAN-US ties in trade, energy transition", "content": "Vietnam recently proposed expanding US-ASEAN cooperation in trade, investment, AI, semiconductors and clean energy as the two sides seek to deepen their Comprehensive Strategic Partnership. \nVietnamese Foreign Minister Le Hoai Trung called for continued US support for Mekong sub-regional cooperation, particularly in water resource management, climate change adaptation and sustainable infrastructure. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/vietnam-calls-for-stronger-asean-us-ties-in-trade-energy-transition-312006-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-23-012", "date": "2026-07-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh PM forms committee to tackle textile sector issues", "content": "Bangladesh PM Tarique Rahman recently formed a high-level committee to review and resolve problems being faced by the country’s textile sector.\nThis followed a meeting between leaders from the Bangladesh Textile Mills Association (BTMA) and Rahman.\nBTMA leaders sought the government’s continued support for the sector’s sustainable development and urged policy support to enhance its global competitiveness.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-pm-forms-committee-to-tackle-textile-sector-issues-312005-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-23-013", "date": "2026-07-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["delay"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India's cotton risk builds as sowing lags and ICE rises", "content": "India’s kharif cotton sowing was 5.97 per cent behind last year at 92.53 lakh hectares as of July 17, with delayed rains affecting key states.\nICE December 2026 cotton rose to 80.42 cents per pound on July 21, adding to raw-material risk for mills.\nDuty-free imports until October 31 may buffer mills, but yarn margins and sourcing costs remain exposed.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-cotton-risk-builds-as-sowing-lags-and-ice-rises-312004-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-23-014", "date": "2026-07-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Dhaka plans to privatise petro products import, power distribution", "content": "Bangladesh is planning to allow the private sector to import petroleum products to reduce the subsidy burden, according to Energy and Mineral Resources Minister Iqbal Hasan Mahmud.\nThe government also plans to privatise power distribution for the same reason, he told a recent discussion on energy security.\nHis ministry has invited private sector proposals to take over electricity distribution companies.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/dhaka-plans-to-privatise-petro-products-import-power-distribution-312003-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-23-015", "date": "2026-07-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Is China+1 dead? How FTAs give India a second chance", "content": "Chief mentor of CMAI, Rahul Mehta said India captured only limited gains from the China+1 sourcing shift as buyers sought greater scale, while Bangladesh and Vietnam advanced faster. \nWith apparel exports at $16.29 billion last year and $4.19 billion in Q1 2026, FTAs offer fresh opportunities, but compliance, labour, quality and scale remain key hurdles.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/is-china-1-dead-how-ftas-give-india-a-second-chance-311993-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-23-016", "date": "2026-07-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["growth", "increase", "decline"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "India’s Arvind Fashions’ Q1 revenue jumps as direct sales strengthen", "content": "India's Arvind Fashions Ltd has reported a 15.5 per cent YoY rise in Q1 FY27 revenue to ₹1,279 crore (~$127.9 million), driven by strong direct-to-consumer channel growth. \nEBITDA increased 19.6 per cent, while PAT declined due to lower other income. \nThe company expects 12-15 per cent revenue growth in FY27 supported by retail expansion, AI adoption and operational efficiencies.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/india-s-arvind-fashions-q1-revenue-jumps-as-direct-sales-strengthen-311989-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-23-017", "date": "2026-07-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "DGFT's RCMC relief proposal limited by ₹10,000 shipment cap", "content": "India's DGFT has proposed waiving RCMC for postal, courier and e-commerce export consignments with FOB value up to ₹10,000 (~$115).\nThe move cuts a fixed compliance cost for micro-exporters, but the low cap may limit any lift for apparel exporters using FTP benefits.\nStakeholders seek a turnover-based route and safeguards before consultation closes on July 30, 2026.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/dgft-s-rcmc-relief-proposal-limited-by-10-000-shipment-cap-311981-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-23-018", "date": "2026-07-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["fast_fashion"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "EU’s €750 mn crackdown puts China’s $42 bn apparel trade on notice", "content": "European Commission penalties totalling €750 million (~$857 million) against AliExpress and Temu push online fashion compliance upstream from parcels to platforms.\nTexPro says extra-EU apparel imports from China rose 17.10 per cent to $42.09 billion in 2025, lifting share to 29.03 per cent.\nSellers and sourcing teams face scrutiny over listing data, seller identities and tariff classifications.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/eu-s-750-mn-crackdown-puts-china-s-42-bn-apparel-trade-on-notice-311969-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
